<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added reserves into the banking system on Wednesday via overnight system repurchase agreements, the New York Fed said.</p>
<p>The operation was expected, since this session is the final day of the maintenance period and federal funds were coming under a bit of pressure.</p>
<p>Federal funds were at 5-1/2 percent, well above the 5-1/4 percent target rate, when the Fed entered the open market.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867</p>
